{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]The earth is the Lord's and all it holds
The world [Gm]and all who live in it
For he founded it upon the seas
And set [Gm]it firm upon the wa[Eb]ters
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Lift [Bb]up your heads, you [Eb]gates
Be [Gm]lifted up, you [Eb]ancient [Bb]doors
That [F]the King of [Gm]glory [Eb]may come in
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Who is this [Bb]King of glory
[Eb/Bb]The Lord, strong and [Gm]mighty
The [F]Lord, mighty [Bb]in battle
[Eb/Bb]Who is he, this King of [Gm]glory
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Lift up [F]your heads, you gates
Be [Bb]lifted up, you ancient [Gm]doors
That the King [Eb]of glo[Bb]ry may [F]come in
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The [Gm]Lord of [Eb]hosts, he is [F]the King of glo[Bb][F]ry
{end_of_verse}

